.TH DIGICARLO-GUI 1 "2026-09-23" "DigiCarlo 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
digicarlo-gui \- the DigiCarlo window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B digicarlo-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window does what \fBdigicarlo\fR(1) does. Cameras and cards appear on the
left as they are plugged in; \fBPull\fR copies their new pictures into the
archive. Waiting shots appear on the right in sessions, each with the date it
will get. Select any shots (shift-click, ctrl-click, or click a session's
heading) and use \fBSet date\fR, \fBCamera's date\fR or \fBAutomatic\fR to
change how they are dated, or \fBLeave out\fR to keep them out of the library.
\fBPut in library\fR writes the re-dated copies.
.PP
The dashboard's speedometer shows how far the current job has got; its
odometer counts every file DigiCarlo has put in the library.
.PP
It needs PyQt6 (\fBpython3-pyqt6\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR digicarlo (1)
